Q: Spring JPA Query as native query with alias and params A: <p>What you are trying to achieve with dynamic query construction doesn't align with Spring Data JPA Query Methods. Spring Data JPA expects to see the fully constructed query during the compile time.</p>
<p>You can provide only parameter values for columns, e.g.:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>@NativeQuery(&quot;from Person p where p.name LIKE ?1&quot;)
Set&lt;Person&gt; customFindByName(String name);
</code></pre>
<p>or</p>
<pre><code>// here @Param is redundant, as Spring Data JPA guesses the parameter name by the variable name
@NativeQuery(&quot;from Person p where p.name LIKE :name&quot;)
Set&lt;Person&gt; customFindByName(@Param(&quot;name&quot;) String name);
</code></pre>
<h1>Solution</h1>
<p>Use <a href="https://docs.spring.io/spring-data/commons/docs/current/api/org/springframework/data/domain/Sort.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Sort</a> to implement sorting by fields dynamically.</p>
<p>Remember, it is all about abstraction in Spring. You don't write SQL yourself, you use an appropriate neat abstraction.</p>
<p>To reduce boilerplate, I use Lombok further.</p>
<p>Given a <code>Person</code> entity:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>@Entity
@Getter
@Setter
@EqualsAndHashCode(onlyExplicitlyIncluded = true)
@ToString
@NoArgsConstructor
public class Person {
  @Id
  @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.UUID)
  private UUID uuid;

  @EqualsAndHashCode.Include
  private String name;

  @EqualsAndHashCode.Include
  private Integer age;

  public Person(String name, Integer age) {
    this.name = name;
    this.age = age;
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>And the <code>PersonRepository</code> repository:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>public interface PersonRepository extends JpaRepository&lt;Person, UUID&gt; {
  @NativeQuery(value = &quot;select * from Person p&quot;)
  List&lt;Person&gt; findAllSortedByField(Sort sort);
}
</code></pre>
<p>You can test it like the following:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>@SpringBootTest
@Transactional
class PersonRepositoryTest {
  @Autowired
  private PersonRepository personRepository;

  @BeforeEach
  void setUp() {
    personRepository.save(new Person(&quot;Adam&quot;, 34));
    personRepository.save(new Person(&quot;Bob&quot;, 22));
    personRepository.save(new Person(&quot;Cale&quot;, 38));
  }

  @Test
  void shouldFindAllSortedByAge() {
    var actual = personRepository.findAllSortedByField(Sort.by(&quot;age&quot;));

    var expected = List.of(
        new Person(&quot;Bob&quot;, 22),
        new Person(&quot;Adam&quot;, 34),
        new Person(&quot;Cale&quot;, 38)
    );
    assertThat(actual).containsExactlyElementsOf(expected);
  }

  @Test
  void shouldFindAllSortedByName() {
    var actual = personRepository.findAllSortedByField(Sort.by(&quot;p.name&quot;).descending());

    var expected = List.of(
        new Person(&quot;Cale&quot;, 38),
        new Person(&quot;Bob&quot;, 22),
        new Person(&quot;Adam&quot;, 34)
    );
    assertThat(actual).containsExactlyElementsOf(expected);
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>There, you can reference values either by column name of by full qualifier of table alias + column name, but it's less stable, as your code now is coupled with the actual query. You can further look into the documentation for different use cases. This is just an example.</p>
<p><code>pom.xml</code> to replicate the test project:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;UTF-8&quot;?&gt;
&lt;project xmlns=&quot;http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0&quot; xmlns:xsi=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance&quot;
         xsi:schemaLocation=&quot;http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd&quot;&gt;
    &lt;modelVersion&gt;4.0.0&lt;/modelVersion&gt;
    &lt;parent&gt;
        &lt;groupId&gt;org.springframework.boot&lt;/groupId&gt;
        &lt;artifactId&gt;spring-boot-starter-parent&lt;/artifactId&gt;
        &lt;version&gt;4.0.1&lt;/version&gt;
        &lt;relativePath/&gt; &lt;!-- lookup parent from repository --&gt;
    &lt;/parent&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;com.example&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;so-jpa-query-parameter&lt;/artifactId&gt;
    &lt;version&gt;0.0.1-SNAPSHOT&lt;/version&gt;

    &lt;properties&gt;
        &lt;java.version&gt;25&lt;/java.version&gt;
    &lt;/properties&gt;

    &lt;dependencies&gt;
        &lt;dependency&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.springframework.boot&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;spring-boot-h2console&lt;/artifactId&gt;
        &lt;/dependency&gt;

        &lt;dependency&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.springframework.boot&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;spring-boot-starter-data-jpa&lt;/artifactId&gt;
        &lt;/dependency&gt;

        &lt;dependency&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;com.h2database&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;h2&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;scope&gt;runtime&lt;/scope&gt;
        &lt;/dependency&gt;

        &lt;dependency&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.springframework.boot&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;spring-boot-starter-data-jpa-test&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;scope&gt;test&lt;/scope&gt;
        &lt;/dependency&gt;

        &lt;dependency&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.assertj&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;assertj-core&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;version&gt;3.27.6&lt;/version&gt;
            &lt;scope&gt;test&lt;/scope&gt;
        &lt;/dependency&gt;

        &lt;dependency&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.projectlombok&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;lombok&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;scope&gt;annotationProcessor&lt;/scope&gt;
        &lt;/dependency&gt;
    &lt;/dependencies&gt;

    &lt;build&gt;
        &lt;plugins&gt;
            &lt;plugin&gt;
                &lt;groupId&gt;org.springframework.boot&lt;/groupId&gt;
                &lt;artifactId&gt;spring-boot-maven-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;/plugin&gt;
        &lt;/plugins&gt;
    &lt;/build&gt;
&lt;/project&gt;

</code></pre>
